      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Until recently, treatment options for those with severe or difficult-to-treat asthma have been restricted to the use of beta 2-agonists and corticosteroids. It has been increasingly recognised that such patients need a new approach. This article discusses how anti-immunoglobulin E treatment could contribute to the successful management of patients with this condition."},
